.TH BIGINTZERO 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntInit, bigIntDestroy, bigIntZero, bigIntReserve, bigIntCopy, bigIntSwap, bigIntNegate, int_32ToBigInt, bigIntFromInt64, bigIntFromString \- manage dynamically allocated signed integers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

void bigIntInit(BigInt *a);
void bigIntDestroy(BigInt *a);
void bigIntZero(BigInt *a);
int bigIntReserve(BigInt *a, size_t limbs);
int bigIntCopy(BigInt *dst, const BigInt *src);
void bigIntSwap(BigInt *a, BigInt *b);
int int_32ToBigInt(BigInt *a, uint32_t val);
int bigIntFromInt64(BigInt *a, int64_t val);
void bigIntNegate(BigInt *a);
int bigIntFromString(BigInt *a, const char *text);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Init initializes a fresh allocation-free zero. BIGINT_INIT is the equivalent
static initializer. Destroy releases storage and restores the initial state;
repeated destruction is safe. Zero sets size to zero and sign to +1,
retaining capacity. Negate changes a nonzero value's sign without allocation;
zero stays positive.
Never call Init on a live allocation without destroying it first.
.PP
Reserve ensures capacity for at least the requested limb count. It grows
geometrically and leaves new inactive limbs uninitialized. Copy deep-copies
the value into an initialized destination; self-copy is supported. Swap
exchanges ownership without allocating. Structure assignment is not a value copy.
.PP
int_32ToBigInt sets an unsigned scalar. FromInt64 sets a signed scalar,
including INT64_MIN without intermediate signed overflow.
FromString accepts ASCII decimal digits with one optional leading + or -.
Empty text is zero; negative zero is canonicalized to positive zero.
A lone sign, spaces, separators and NULL text are invalid.
Parsing is transactional and leaves the previous value unchanged on error.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Init, Destroy, Zero, Negate and Swap return void. Other functions return 0 on success,
-1 on allocation failure, INT_MAX on an unrepresentable size, or -2 for invalid
decimal input. Errors leave the destination unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
